TEXT 64 32 Left 2 ;Voltage divider: loading error
TEXT 64 656 Left 2 !.tran 0 1m 0 1u
TEXT 64 704 Left 2 ;Without a load VOUT = 2.5 V. With RLOAD = 100k, VOUT is about 2.38 V.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 ;1. Click Run: the running-person button at the top left.
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 ;2. On the schematic, click the wire labeled VOUT (not the component).
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 ;3. Click the VIN wire too, to compare input and output in the same plot.
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 ;If the plot is empty, select the schematic window and click the labeled wire again.
TEXT 64 968 Left 2 ;EXPERIMENTS AND COMMON QUESTIONS
TEXT 64 1008 Left 2 ;Right-click a component to edit its value. Predict first, change one value, then Run.
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;TRY: Change RLOAD from 100k to 10k, then 1k.
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 ;FAQ: The lower divider resistor is in parallel with the load.
TEXT 64 1128 Left 2 ;Lower load resistance pulls VOUT below the unloaded 2.5 V.
TEXT 64 1168 Left 2 ;TRY: Change R1 and R2 together from 10k to 1k; loading error gets smaller.
TEXT 64 1208 Left 2 ;The trade-off is increased divider current and power consumption.
